      article.main
        h1 Includes
        p Includes allow you to insert the contents of one Pug file into another.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="0")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="456366491")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  //- index.pug
                  doctype html
                  html
                    include includes/head.pug
                    body
                      h1 My Site
                      p Welcome to my super lame site.
                      include includes/foot.pug
              div(data-reactid="5")
                textarea(data-reactid="6").
                  //- includes/head.pug
                  head
                    title My Site
                    script(src='/javascripts/jquery.js')
                    script(src='/javascripts/app.js')
              div(data-reactid="7")
                textarea(data-reactid="8").
                  //- includes/foot.pug
                  footer#footer
                    p Copyright (c) foobar
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="9")
              div(data-reactid="10")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="11").
                  <!DOCTYPE html>
                  <html>
                  
                  <head>
                    <title>My Site</title>
                    <script src="/javascripts/jquery.js"></script>
                    <script src="/javascripts/app.js"></script>
                  </head>
                  
                  <body>
                    <h1>My Site</h1>
                    <p>Welcome to my super lame site.</p>
                    <footer id="footer">
                      <p>Copyright (c) foobar</p>
                    </footer>
                  </body>
                  
                  </html>
        p
          | If the path is absolute (e.g.,
          code include /root.pug
          | ), it is resolved by prepending
          code options.basedir
          | . Otherwise, paths are resolved relative to the current file being compiled.
        p
          | If no file extension is given,
          code .pug
          | is automatically appended to the file name.
        h2#including-plain-text
          | Including Plain Text
          a.header-anchor(href="#including-plain-text", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p Including non-Pug files simply includes their raw text.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="1")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="80432334")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  //- index.pug
                  doctype html
                  html
                    head
                      style
                        include style.css
                    body
                      h1 My Site
                      p Welcome to my super lame site.
                      script
                        include script.js
              div(data-reactid="5")
                textarea(data-reactid="6").
                  /* style.css */
                  h1 {
                    color: red;
                  }
              div(data-reactid="7")
                textarea(data-reactid="8").
                  // script.js
                  console.log('You are awesome');
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="9")
              div(data-reactid="10")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="11").
                  <!DOCTYPE html>
                  <html>
                  
                  <head>
                    <style>
                      /* style.css */
                      h1 {
                        color: red;
                      }
                    </style>
                  </head>
                  
                  <body>
                    <h1>My Site</h1>
                    <p>Welcome to my super lame site.</p>
                    <script>
                      // script.js
                      console.log('You are awesome');
                    </script>
                  </body>
                  
                  </html>
        h2#including-filtered-text
          | Including Filtered Text
          a.header-anchor(href="#including-filtered-text", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p You can combine filters with includes, allowing you to filter things as you include them.
        div
